- Camera lives here: `camera_shift` is a screen-pixel vector, `camera_zoom` an
- isotropic scalar. $mol_touch drives both from pointer, wheel and pinch.
$bog_vmap_app_pane $mol_view
	scene_uri \
	doc_src \
	doc_css \
	- Canvas placement of free parts, world coordinates keyed by property name.
	- Never joined with `doc_css`: that one is the document, this one is the desk.
	- Two way: dragging a node on the canvas writes here.
	spots? *
	- Property name of the picked node, `null` when nothing is picked.
	selected? null
	doc_js *
	doc_root \
	- Sources of the land libraries, compiled by the scene before the document.
	- On the bridge and not in `scene_uri`: a change of lands is a recompile, a
	- change of pack is a reload, see section 5.
	libs /$bog_vmap_bridge_part
	- Whether the overlay may be cut open under the picked part. The host turns
	- this off while something is carried from the palette: that gesture has no
	- pointer capture, so a release over the hole would land in the frame and the
	- host would never hear of the drop.
	hole_allowed true
	handshake? 0
	ready false
	- The scene owes an answer to something we sent and has stopped answering.
	- Set by the watchdog, cleared by the next message from the scene.
	stalled? false
	error_at*? \
	error \
	isolation \
	camera_shift? $mol_vector_2d<number> /
		0
		0
	camera_zoom? 1
	- Which frame is live. Bumped by `scene_restart`: a new key is a new frame
	- element, so a stuck scene is replaced rather than talked to.
	scene_generation? 0
	Scene* $bog_vmap_app_pane_frame
		uri <= scene_uri
	sub /
		<= Overlay $bog_vmap_app_pane_overlay
			style <= overlay_style *
			frame_showed <= frame_showed false
			frame_style <= frame_style *
			press? <=> node_press? null
			move? <=> node_move? null
			release? <=> node_release? null
	plugins /
		^
		<= Touch $mol_touch
			allow_draw false
			allow_pan true
			allow_zoom true
			pan? <=> camera_shift?
			zoom? <=> camera_zoom?

- Transparent gate over the frame. It swallows every pointer event and lets it
- bubble up to the pane, where $mol_touch listens: there are no editor modes, one
- layer takes every gesture. A click that does not move is relayed to the scene
- as `click_at`, and under the picked part the layer is cut open, so that one
- part at a time gets real events. Hover on any other part does not work, and
- that is the accepted price of the overlay owning the input.
-
- Selection is drawn HERE and not in the scene: the overlay belongs to the host,
- so no code inside the document can fake a selection frame or hide one, and the
- ring stays crisp because the camera scales the scene, not this layer.
- @see ../../ARCHITECTURE.md section 4
$bog_vmap_app_pane_overlay $mol_view
	frame_showed false
	frame_style *
	press? null
	move? null
	release? null
	event *
		^
		pointerdown? <=> press? null
		pointermove? <=> move? null
		pointerup? <=> release? null
	- Ring around the picked node. A free part of the class, put into `sub` only
	- while something is picked, so an empty canvas costs no node at all.
	- The handles sit outside the box, on the strip of overlay that still takes
	- the pointer, and say where the part can be taken hold of.
	Frame $mol_view
		style <= frame_style *
		sub /
			<= Handle_nw $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \nw
			<= Handle_ne $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \ne
			<= Handle_sw $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \sw
			<= Handle_se $bog_vmap_app_pane_handle corner \se

- A grip at one corner of the ring. Picture only, like the ring: the press it
- marks is taken by the overlay under it.
$bog_vmap_app_pane_handle $mol_view
	corner \
	attr *
		^
		bog_vmap_app_pane_handle_corner <= corner

- `sandbox` goes FIRST: $mol_dom_render_attributes writes the object in key order,
- and an iframe that got its src before its sandbox is already loading unsandboxed.
$bog_vmap_app_pane_frame $mol_frame
	attr *
		sandbox \allow-scripts
		^
